messages:
mike_s: escalating a customer streaming issue — Node/Edge runtime (Vercel). Using @redwood/sdk v1.4.2. Remote ReadableStream hangs after ~10-30s when token rotation happens. They see a 401 in control plane logs then the client never resumes. Repro steps below.

iliana: any hints about retries? v1.5 changed some retry semantics for streaming. Could be double-retry + edge environment causing closed body reader.

mike_s: we tried pinning to v1.3.9 and it looked more stable, but the customer needs features in 1.4.x. Repro:
```ts
// edge runtime (vercel) minimal repro
import Redwood from '@redwood/sdk';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'redwood-1.0', input: 'stream test' });
const reader = stream.body!.getReader();
while(true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  // process chunk
}
```
Logs: control-plane shows: 2026-03-09T12:10:05Z "auth: token rotated for tenant X" then 2026-03-09T12:10:05Z "request 0xabc -> 401" and client-side stops receiving chunks (no error thrown).

kevin_p: that pattern smells like the SDK's automatic retry is swallowing the 401 and not re-establishing SSE/stream properly on edge. Do you have network proxies (like a CDN or Vercel edge function) that might close idle sockets when upstream auth resets?

mike_s: it's an edge function on Vercel (edge runtime), no extra CDN. We saw an error in the app logs: `ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE` and occasionally `TypeError: Failed to execute 'read' on 'ReadableStreamDefaultReader': stream is locked`.

iliana: can you include headers present when the 401 happens? Specifically Authorization and any x-retry-id. Also which fetch polyfill is used (native edge fetch vs node fetch/undici).

mike_s: customer confirmed native edge fetch. Sample headers from the failed request: `authorization: Bearer ey...` then next request after rotation had no auth header for ~100ms window (rotation job). SDK emits a retry with no auth and control-plane returns 401.

kevin_p: immediate mitigation: disable streaming auto-retry in the SDK on edge or set REDWOOD_EDGE_STREAM_RETRY=off for now. We'll also try a patch that ensures token refresh is atomic and queued while stream is active. Can you test with env override?

mike_s: tried env override REDWOOD_EDGE_STREAM_RETRY=false on customer's env — stream survives rotation in our short tests. Customer reported no duplicate charges in that mode.

iliana: created internal bug: ENG-RUNTIME-789. Root cause hypothesis: racing token refresh + retry wrapper in v1.4.x produces a transient unauthenticated followup request which then leaves the ReadableStream reader in an inconsistent state on edge runtime. v1.3.x didn't have the streaming retry wrapper, v1.5 has a different fix but not fully release-tested.

support-bot: ticket S-26432 created and linked to ENG-RUNTIME-789, priority P1, assigned to eng-runtime.

kevin_p: follow-ups: ask customer to (1) set REDWOOD_EDGE_STREAM_RETRY=false as workaround, (2) upgrade to the next nightly we push — it will queue token refreshes for active streams, and (3) share more logs if they hit duplicate billing or multiple uploads.

mike_s: copying customer response: tried the env flag, stable for 24h. They will hold off on upgrade until we provide a build. I'll keep this thread updated. :thumbsup:
